# CoW 2G — index-assign on a bare param inside a loop. `xs[0] = xs[0] + 1`
# peels to a DOTLESS root (`xs`), which the prescan's Assign arm dropped before
# the 2G hardening (the `@mut:` path requires a dot; a bare-param index target
# has none). With the dotless-root insert the loop-carried materialize fires and
# the write persists across iterations. Expect 13 (10 + 3), caller stays 10.
#
# In known_gaps/ (out of the runtime-diff corpus) pending the self-host CoW-2G
# mirror closing the same index-root recording hole. Rust lane is correct.
void h(Vector[int] xs):
    int i = 0
    while i < 3:
        xs[0] = xs[0] + 1
        i = i + 1
    print(xs[0])

void main():
    Vector[int] a = [10]
    h(a)
    print(a[0])
